# CODEOWNERS routes review by RISK, not by volume.
# The security owner is pulled in only when sensitive files change.
#
# Syntax: <path pattern>  <owner(s)>
# In a real org these would be @org/security-team, @org/platform-team.

# Default: everything needs a review from the repo owner.
*                               @timiajose

# The pipeline itself is privileged - a PR that edits these could delete
# its own gates. Changing them must be reviewed deliberately.
/.github/workflows/             @timiajose
/.github/CODEOWNERS             @timiajose

# Policy-as-code rules: weakening a guard rule weakens every future PR.
/week-03/pipeline/rules.guard   @timiajose

# Anything that grants AWS permissions.
**/policies/                    @timiajose
**/iam-policies/                @timiajose
**/*trust*.json                 @timiajose
**/*role*.json                  @timiajose
